[3] Transfer dictionary
  finite monodromy         -> finite wall family / descending quotient atom
  almost all primes p      -> persistent denominator/fiber ladder tests
  p-curvature vanishes     -> blocked ledger is compatible under carry/Frobenius lifts
  nonzero p-curvature      -> a denominator witness or Bprime/owner-private opening appears
  operator (D+A)^p         -> marked support: Pisano class + 13-clock + divisor fiber + owner
  naive A^p                -> raw q-blocked scalar, too lossy

[4] Proposed LRC14 p-curvature principle
  If a primitive LRC14 row blocks the fibered ladder for a long range,
  its blocker data should define compatible local sections under q -> p*q
  and q -> d*m fiber maps.  Compatibility is rare: it should force AP,
  Vstar, 2AP, or a lower resource via Bprime(any runner)/owner-private
  deletion.  Incompatibility is a nonzero curvature certificate, i.e. a
  finite denominator witness.

